\details{
Provides methods for retrieving market data from Binance's Spot trading API,
including exchange info, klines, tickers, orderbooks, trade history, and
24-hour statistics.

Inherits from \link{BinanceBase}. All methods support both synchronous and
asynchronous execution depending on the \code{async} parameter at construction.
\subsection{Purpose and Scope}{
\itemize{
\item \strong{Exchange Info}: Retrieve trading pair metadata including precision, filters, and trading status.
\item \strong{Tickers}: Access real-time price data for individual symbols or all pairs.
\item \strong{Order Books}: Get order book depth snapshots.
\item \strong{Trade History}: Retrieve recent trades for any symbol.
\item \strong{24hr Statistics}: Get rolling 24-hour market statistics.
\item \strong{Klines}: Fetch historical candlestick data.
\item \strong{Server Time}: Get exchange server time for clock synchronisation.
}
}

\subsection{Usage}{

All methods are public endpoints requiring no authentication.
}

